---
What a guestbook entry is, and the rules it has to follow.

This is a `commons`: plain types and pure functions, with no state and no access
to the outside world. That makes it the easiest part of the app to test.
---
commons guestbook.entries

--- Who signed: between 1 and 40 characters.
type Name = String where NonEmpty && MaxLength(40)

--- What they wrote: between 1 and 280 characters.
type Message = String where NonEmpty && MaxLength(280)

--- One signature in the guestbook.
type Entry = {
	name: Name,
	message: Message,
}

--- An entry as a single line of text, for a page or a log.
fn signed(entry: Entry) -> String {
	"\"\(entry.message)\" — \(entry.name)"
}
